abstract: >-
  The Dynamic AI Compute Demand Model (DACDM) is a conceptual research framework
  for analyzing AI compute demand as a dynamic interaction between workload growth,
  task complexity, model and hardware efficiency, complexity migration, and
  substitution across execution pathways. Version 1.0 is a conceptual working-paper
  framework and has not been empirically validated.
